# Secrets and credentials. These patterns guard this repository's own small
# surface (the root documents, .github/, .claude/) against accident; nothing
# authored here should ever hold a credential.
#
# The vendored trees under <org>/<repo>/ are upstream bytes, and some of them
# legitimately carry files these patterns match: keystore and TLS test
# fixtures, test-network node keys, a sample .env. They are tracked, and an
# ignore pattern never affects a tracked file, so nothing here hides or alters
# them. Two consequences:
#
# - `git subtree add` stages a corpus with read-tree, which no ignore pattern
#   reaches, so a vendored tree always arrives whole.
# - An extraction is staged with `git add`, which silently drops any file a
#   pattern matches. Verify every extraction against its source in both
#   directions after staging it.
#
# Verify coverage BY EFFECT, never by reading these patterns, and calibrate
# every sweep against a path that must NOT be ignored:
#
#   git -c core.excludesFile=/dev/null check-ignore --no-index -q -- .env      && echo ignored || echo "NOT ignored"
#   git -c core.excludesFile=/dev/null check-ignore --no-index -q -- README.md && echo "check is broken" || echo "check discriminates"
#
# A check that cannot report "not ignored" is not checking anything.
#
# No pattern here may match a tracked file OUTSIDE the vendored trees. After
# any change to this file, this must print nothing:
#
#   git -c core.excludesFile=/dev/null ls-files -ci --exclude-standard -- ':(glob)*' ':(glob).github/**' ':(glob).claude/**'
#
# The same command without the pathspecs lists the vendored matches, by design.

# Environment and credentials
.env
.env.*
# The example CLASS, not one filename: .env.local.example is a template and must
# reach a clone. End-anchored, so .env.example.local stays ignored. Do not narrow.
!.env*.example
*.env
.envrc
credentials.json
service-account.json
*.credentials
secrets/
.secrets/
*.secret
.netrc
.git-credentials

# Keys and certificates
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.ppk
id_rsa
id_dsa
id_ecdsa
id_ed25519
secring.gpg

# Wallets, keystores and node keys. UTC--* is the name geth gives a keystore
# file, which can land outside any keystore/ directory. A client run from a
# vendored tree writes a node key and an engine JWT secret into its data
# directory.
keystore/
*.keystore
UTC--*
wallet.json
mnemonic.txt
*.nodekey
node.key
etc-node.key
jwt.hex
jwtsecret

# Package-registry auth. These carry registry tokens, and nothing here needs a
# registry, so the safe posture is to ignore them outright.
.npmrc
.yarnrc
.yarnrc.yml

# Machine-local working state. `.local/` is this repository's private working
# directory (plans, prompts, drafts, scratch scripts) and never reaches a clone.
.local/
CLAUDE.local.md
SESSION_NOTES.md
PLANNING.md
SCRATCH.md
*.scratch.*
*.draft.*

# Agent-written and per-developer state. The rest of `.claude/` is TRACKED on
# purpose: an agent, skill or rule inside an ignored directory never reaches a
# clone, which is not a stricter form of sharing it.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/agent-memory-local/
.claude/launch.json
.claude/scheduled_tasks.json
.claude/**/*.local.*
.claude/**/*-local/

# OS and editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
.vscode/settings.json
.idea/
